+### 4.3 list_conversations
+
+Requests a page of the authenticated user's conversation summaries, newest activity first.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "list_conversations",
+  "limit": 25,
+  "before": {
+    "updatedAt": "2026-09-30T08:00:00.000Z",
+    "sessionId": "s1"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+| Field    | Type               | Required | Description                                                                 |
+| -------- | ------------------ | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`   | string             | Yes      | `"list_conversations"`                                                      |
+| `limit`  | number             | No       | Positive integer from 1 to 200; when omitted, the store applies its default |
+| `before` | ConversationCursor | No       | Exclusive cursor `{updatedAt, sessionId}` for paging older conversations    |
+
+Validation and dispatch:
+
+- `validateMessage` accepts `list_conversations` regardless of server configuration, drops undeclared fields such as `userId`, and rejects an invalid `limit` (outside integer `1..200`) or malformed `before` cursor (`{updatedAt, sessionId}` with a parseable ISO `updatedAt` and string `sessionId`) with `INVALID_MESSAGE` naming the field ([validated by: validates list_conversations frames, cursor shapes, and rejects invalid fields naming the field](../../src/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L82)).
+- `list_conversations` runs outside the per-session turn lock alongside `ping`, so a request sent while a `user_message` is streaming on the same session is answered before that turn's `stream_end` ([validated by: answers list_conversations before stream_end while a user_message is streaming on the same session](../../src/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L235)).
 
